    <ferc:UnappropriatedRetainedEarnings id="f-507" contextRef="c-31" unitRef="u-02" decimals="0">-4454227</ferc:UnappropriatedRetainedEarnings>
    <ferc:AdditionalInformationOnFieldsWhereTheRespondentOperatesTextblock id="f-509" contextRef="c-20">&lt;p&gt;The respondent operates a high-pressure natural gas transmission line in the Northern DJ Basin consisting of approximately 16 miles of 6&amp;quot; steel and 14 miles of 8&amp;quot; steel. The pipeline extends from Laramie County, WY to northern Weld County CO, of which approximately 26 miles are located in Wyoming and 4 miles in Colorado.&lt;/p&gt;</ferc:AdditionalInformationOnFieldsWhereTheRespondentOperatesTextblock>
    <ferc:DescriptionOfPlantAndOperationsOfRespondentTextblock id="f-510" contextRef="c-20">&lt;p&gt;The respondent does not operate any plants. The operations are limited to the high-pressure transportation of natural gas only.&lt;/p&gt;</ferc:DescriptionOfPlantAndOperationsOfRespondentTextblock>
    <ferc:DetailsOfAnyChangesOfScopeInRespondentsOperationsTextblock id="f-511" contextRef="c-20">&lt;p&gt;There have been no significant changes in the respondent's scope of operations during the year.&lt;/p&gt;</ferc:DetailsOfAnyChangesOfScopeInRespondentsOperationsTextblock>
    <ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock id="f-512" contextRef="c-20">&lt;p&gt;Currently, the respondent (RFIGT) has one firm service customer, Kaiser-Frontier Midstream, LLC (KFM). The parent entity of RFIGT, Roaring Fork Midstream, LLC (RFM) acquired KFM in June 2025. Additionally, RFIGT provides interruptible service to RFM. Both RFM and KFM are affiliates of RFIGT.&lt;/p&gt;</ferc:GeneralInformationOnPlantAndOperationsTextblock>
